 "notes": "An implicit key is on one line and at most 1024 characters long, counting the quotes. The first key is a space and 1022 letters: it needs quotes, so it is written as 1025 characters. The second is 600 single quotes: single-quoted it is 1202 characters (each quote doubled), but double-quoted it is 602, so either the short form or the explicit `? ` form is right. The third is 1025 letters, which is too long even without quotes. A writer must use the explicit form (or another form of at most 1024 characters) and never write an implicit key that a reader has to refuse. The kit checks the length itself, because a lenient reader accepts a long key. This is a writing convention of the family, not the specification: a string is written plain only when every common reader reads it as that same string, so the text is judged under the YAML 1.2 Core schema (loose) and also under YAML 1.1 and the number forms common readers accept (strict).",
 "provenance": {
